`desktop/src/state/drawioXml.ts` is derived from that project's
`lib/utils.ts`. The draw.io XML validator, its helper checks and
`wrapWithMxFile` were ported and adapted; the diagnostic message text is
kept verbatim because those strings are read by an agent. The upstream
`autoFixXml` repair pass was deliberately NOT ported — see that file's
header for why.

`desktop/src/state/drawioOps.ts` is derived from the same file's
`applyDiagramOperations`. What is taken is the design — the
`{operation, cell_id, new_xml}` grammar, the rule that `new_xml`'s own id
must match `cell_id`, the delete cascade over children and referencing
edges, the protection of draw.io's root cells — together with several
diagnostic sentences verbatim, for the same reason. The implementation is
not a port: upstream applies a batch partially and re-serializes through
the DOM, and this one is all-or-nothing and edits the document as text so
that bytes outside the named cells survive. See that file's header.

`desktop/electron/src/authorguide/shapes/` is a verbatim copy of that
project's `docs/shape-libraries/` at commit
6e653942b0a9912123093179c6f2db2cf7c1d42f — 31 files documenting the
draw.io shape libraries, which upstream derived in turn from
jgraph/drawio's own Apache-2.0 shape data. The directory is unmodified,
so it can be diffed against upstream directly; the corrections we serve
on top of it (a scraping artifact removed, an index rebuilt from the
files that exist, a stated count of what each file enumerates) live in
`gen-shapes.ts` and are documented there.

`desktop/electron/src/authorguide/guides.ts` adapts the layout and
edge-routing rules from that project's `lib/system-prompts.ts` for the
`author_guide {kind:'diagram', topic:'layout'}` topic. Upstream's tool
names, its "no wrapper tags" rule and its ban on XML comments were NOT
carried over: all three describe upstream's own pipeline and are untrue
here, where every document level is normalised on the way in and the
`ops` path preserves comments.

